===Etymology===
{{acronym|en}} of its original name, {{m|en|[[United Nations]] [[international|International]] [[child|Children's]] [[emergency|Emergency]] [[fund|Fund]]}}. Now officially ''United Nations Children's Fund''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈju.niˌsɛf/|a=US}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# An agency of the [[United Nations]] responsible for providing [[humanitarian]] and [[development aid|developmental aid]] to [[child]]ren worldwide.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1951|chapter=Contributions to the United Nations International Children’s Emergency Fund ('''UNICEF''')—H.&nbsp;R. 2785|title=Survey of Activities of the Committee on Foreign Affairs, House of Representatives, Eighty-first Congress (January 3, 1949–January 2, 1951)|location=Washington, D.C.|publisher=[[w:United States Government Publishing Office|United States Government Printing Office]]|section=section I (Strengthening United States Participation in International Organizations)|page=16|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/sim_united-states-congress-hearings-prints-and-reports_january-03-1949-january-02-1951/page/16/mode/1up|oclc=66280811|passage=The '''UNICEF''' was established in December 1946 by resolution of the United Nations General Assembly. {{...}} To present an adequate picture of the problem which the Committee on Foreign Affairs faced during the Eighty-first Congress in connection with the '''UNICEF''', the background of congressional action in the Eightieth Congress is necessary.}}

====Usage notes====
* Formerly used with ''the'' (i.e., as ''the UNICEF'').

